        <item>
            <title>1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:37:25 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1070</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } .when, .earlier { color: #9a9a9a; } hr { border-color: #444; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 4px; }
.when { font-weight: 400; color: #777; }
.earlier { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #777; margin: 18px 0 2px; }
hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin: 16px 0 0; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1070) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases play smoothly from the start.</b> The sound stays steady and in step, playback waits until enough has loaded, and the timeline shows what&#8217;s loaded.</li>
<li>Showcases ask for your name once, not twice.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1061) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcase links you are sent</b> now show a moving preview in email and in chat, and a personal link opens straight to its player.</li>
<li>Small fixes to how showcases are shared.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1059) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Who watched your showcase.</b> Each showcase now reports how it was watched: who opened it, when, from where and on what; how far they got and whether they finished; the moments people replayed; full screen and sound. The Review Manager shows a watch-through curve, the most-watched moments, and every visit, with <b>Export Viewing CSV&#8230;</b>. Asobi tells you when someone opens it and when they finish.</li>
<li><b>Forwarded links ask who is watching.</b> When a person&#8217;s link is opened on another device, the new viewer is asked for their name and email before it plays, so a forward becomes a named viewer.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1058) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcase links.</b> <b>Review &#9656; Make Showcase&#8230;</b> makes a link for showing work, not reviewing it: a splash with the title and a play button, a plain player, and a closing card with your contact and a button to your website. Links live on show.byautonomy.com; name the people it is for and each gets their own link. Who watched, and how much, arrives in the next update.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1053) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Watch the speed.</b> The Network window shows the speed as it is measured, with a line of it over the test, green when fast, amber in between, red when slow, and the peak.</li>
<li><b>Thorough Test.</b> Six seconds of eight downloads at once, for a steadier number on a fast line (uses up to 400 MB). <b>Measure Now</b> stays quick.</li>
<li><b>Halation remembers.</b> Switching halation off and on in the Film Lab brings back your settings.</li>
<li><b>A note in the shortcuts.</b> While you type in a text box or note field, letter keys type; press Enter (or the &#10003;) or Esc to get the shortcuts back.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1051) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>A truer connection measurement.</b> <b>Review &#9656; Network &#9656; Measure Now</b> read far too low on fast lines (11 Mbps on a gigabit connection): it timed one small download including the connection setup. It now warms the connection, times only the data arriving, and fills a fast line with four downloads at once. The number is the speed to the review server, which is what fetching media gets; a speed test to a nearby server can read higher.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1050) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Each tool keeps its colour.</b> Circle in red, switch to Text and type in white, go back to the circle and it is red again. A colour picked with no tool in hand goes to the next tool you pick.</li>
<li><b>T is Text.</b> As in every paint program and on the web page. Trim handles moved to <b>&#8679;T</b>.</li>
<li><b>A tick to place text.</b> The text box has a &#10003; beside its size buttons; Enter still works.</li>
<li><b>Line opacity that works.</b> It now changes a selected mark, and picking a colour keeps it instead of resetting to solid. Line width, line opacity and fill opacity open as small pop-ups from the palette, and any line width is one pop-up away after the presets. The web toolbar has line opacity too.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1048) <span class="when">Sep 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The brief stays with its review.</b> A review brief no longer carries over to other clips or to the next launch; it belongs to the review it was written for. The card only opens over a review.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
